  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The abstract does not provide empirical results, quantitative metrics, or details on a specific physical deployment of the framework.",
      "what": "The paper presents a framework combining the Wishes, Interests, and Needs (WIN) co-design methodology with an Urban Living Lab approach to integrate user-generated data and volunteered urban sensing into local planning. The combined method structures how diverse residents contribute local knowledge and everyday experiences to shape smart-city technologies.",
      "why": "It establishes a structured, participatory pathway to prevent technocratic smart-city deployments from reinforcing existing digital divides, ensuring marginalized groups can actively influence urban digital infrastructure."
